      <Id>TH68</Id>
      <ShortTitle>An adversary may gain unauthorized access to resources in Service Fabric</ShortTitle>
      <Category>S</Category>
      <Description>If a service fabric cluster is not secured, it allow any anonymous user to connect to it if it exposes management endpoints to the public Internet.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>If a service fabric cluster is not secured, it allow any anonymous user to connect to it if it exposes management endpoints to the public Internet.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Severity</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>High</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Restrict anonymous access to Service Fabric Cluster. Refer: &lt;a href="https://aka.ms/tmtauthn#anon-access-cluster"&gt;
https://aka.ms/tmtauthn#anon-access-cluster&lt;/a&gt;</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>List of possbile mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>SDL Phase</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Implementation</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The Security Development Lifecycle Phase to be implemented.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Documentation</Name>
          <Label>Documentation</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>https://azure.microsoft.com/documentation/articles/service-fabric-cluster-security</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Link to documentation</Description>
          <Id>Documentation</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Steps</Name>
          <Label>Steps</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Clusters should always be secured to prevent unauthorized users from connecting to your cluster, especially when it has production workloads running on it. While creating a service fabric cluster, ensure that the security mode is set to &amp;quot;secure&amp;quot; and configure the required X.509 server certificate. Creating an &amp;quot;insecure&amp;quot; cluster will allow any anonymous user to connect to it if it exposes management endpoints to the public Internet.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Perscriptive guidance on how to implement mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Steps</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Effort</Name>
          <Label>Effort</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Medium</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The level of effort to apply mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Effort</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
