      <Id>TH425</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Fabric IQ ontology callers may rely on cached resolution that lags behind ontology revisions, producing answers grounded in stale relationships</ShortTitle>
      <Category>S</Category>
      <Description>Ontology resolution in Fabric IQ involves entity bindings, relationship definitions, and cached query plans. When a steward updates the ontology to reflect a corrected relationship or a removed binding, in-flight callers, cached plans, and downstream Data Agents may continue to resolve the prior version for some interval. During that interval, identical queries from different callers can produce different answers, and the answer presented may not match the current authoritative ontology.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Ontology resolution in Fabric IQ involves entity bindings, relationship definitions, and cached query plans. When a steward updates the ontology to reflect a corrected relationship or a removed binding, in-flight callers, cached plans, and downstream Data Agents may continue to resolve the prior version for some interval. During that interval, identical queries from different callers can produce different answers, and the answer presented may not match the current authoritative ontology.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Severity</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Medium</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Document the ontology update propagation interval. For changes intended as access-control or correctness fixes, communicate the propagation window to callers. Where strict consistency matters, route through a path that bypasses cache. Surface the ontology version evaluated alongside each answer.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>List of possbile mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>SDL Phase</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Design</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The Security Development Lifecycle Phase to be implemented.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Documentation</Name>
          <Label>Documentation</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/iq/overview</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Link to documentation</Description>
          <Id>Documentation</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Steps</Name>
          <Label>Steps</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Test the propagation interval by updating an ontology and timing when callers see the change. Document the result.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Perscriptive guidance on how to implement mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Steps</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
