      <Id>TH105</Id>
      <ShortTitle>An adversary can tamper critical database securables and deny the action</ShortTitle>
      <Category>T</Category>
      <Description>An adversary can tamper critical database securables and deny the action</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>An adversary can tamper critical database securables and deny the action</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Severity</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>High</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Add digital signature to critical database securables. Refer: &lt;a href="https://aka.ms/tmtcrypto#securables-db"&gt;
https://aka.ms/tmtcrypto#securables-db&lt;/a&gt;</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>List of possbile mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>SDL Phase</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Implementation</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The Security Development Lifecycle Phase to be implemented.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Documentation</Name>
          <Label>Documentation</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>https://msdn.microsoft.com/library/ms181700</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Link to documentation</Description>
          <Id>Documentation</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Steps</Name>
          <Label>Steps</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>In cases where the integrity of a critical database securable has to be verified, digital signatures should be used. Database securables such as a stored procedure, function, assembly, or trigger can be digitally signed. Below is an example of when this can be useful: Let us say an ISV (Independent Software Vendor) has provided support to a software delivered to one of their customers. Before providing support, the ISV would want to ensure that a database securable in the software was not tampered either by mistake or by a malicious attempt. If the securable is digitally signed, the ISV can verify its digital signature and validate its integrity.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Perscriptive guidance on how to implement mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Steps</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Effort</Name>
          <Label>Effort</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Low</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The level of effort to apply mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Effort</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
