            <Value>Coding agents read every file in scope - source, READMEs, docstrings, comments, dependency package manifests, vendored code, web pages opened during research. Any of these can contain instructions targeting the agent (e.g., a comment in a dependency telling the agent to exfiltrate environment variables, or a README instructing the agent to add a backdoor). Because the developer trusts the agent, malicious code edits or commands flowing from injected instructions are likely to be applied or run.</Value>
          </Values>
