      <Id>TH208</Id>
      <ShortTitle>An LLM agent may repudiate actions due to missing tool-invocation audit trail</ShortTitle>
      <Category>R</Category>
      <Description>When an autonomous or semi-autonomous agent invokes tools — write APIs, code execution, file modification, ticket creation, payments — without recording the chain of reasoning, tool name, arguments, principal on whose behalf the call was made, and the resulting output, there is no reliable record of which entity caused which side effect. This makes after-the-fact attribution, rollback, and dispute resolution impossible.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>When an autonomous or semi-autonomous agent invokes tools — write APIs, code execution, file modification, ticket creation, payments — without recording the chain of reasoning, tool name, arguments, principal on whose behalf the call was made, and the resulting output, there is no reliable record of which entity caused which side effect. This makes after-the-fact attribution, rollback, and dispute resolution impossible.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Severity</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>High</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Log every tool call with: invoking user/session, agent identity, tool name and version, full argument set, tool result, and the model turn that produced the call. Persist logs to an append-only store. Where actions are high-impact (financial, destructive, irreversible), require a human-in-the-loop confirmation that is itself logged.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>List of possbile mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>SDL Phase</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Design</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The Security Development Lifecycle Phase to be implemented.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Documentation</Name>
          <Label>Documentation</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm08-excessive-agency/</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Link to documentation</Description>
          <Id>Documentation</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Steps</Name>
          <Label>Steps</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>List every tool and write-capable function exposed to the agent. For each, define the audit record schema and storage location. Confirm that audit writes are not conditional on agent success and cannot be suppressed by the agent itself.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Perscriptive guidance on how to implement mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Steps</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
