      <Id>TH252</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Tenant-level Fabric settings may permit data egress (cross-geo AI processing, external sharing, exports) inconsistent with data classification</ShortTitle>
      <Category>I</Category>
      <Description>Several Fabric capabilities are gated by tenant-level switches: Cross-geo processing for AI, Cross-geo storing for AI, Power BI semantic models via XMLA endpoints, external user sharing, Copilot/Azure OpenAI integration, and dataset export. When a tenant administrator enables one of these for a single workload's convenience, the change applies tenant-wide and may cause regulated data in unrelated workspaces to leave its intended region or be shared externally without the data owner's knowledge.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Several Fabric capabilities are gated by tenant-level switches: Cross-geo processing for AI, Cross-geo storing for AI, Power BI semantic models via XMLA endpoints, external user sharing, Copilot/Azure OpenAI integration, and dataset export. When a tenant administrator enables one of these for a single workload's convenience, the change applies tenant-wide and may cause regulated data in unrelated workspaces to leave its intended region or be shared externally without the data owner's knowledge.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Severity</Label>
