      <Id>TH362</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Adding external guests to SaaS work management workspaces may grant broader visibility than the inviting user expected</ShortTitle>
      <Category>I</Category>
      <Description>Inviting an external guest to a Jira project, Monday board, Notion workspace, or Trello board frequently grants the guest visibility to more than the specific item they were invited to: cross-references, linked tickets, mentions in unrelated discussions, and search results often surface other workspace content to a guest who has 'access to one thing.' The inviter's mental model of 'I shared one ticket with this contractor' may not match what the guest can actually see.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Inviting an external guest to a Jira project, Monday board, Notion workspace, or Trello board frequently grants the guest visibility to more than the specific item they were invited to: cross-references, linked tickets, mentions in unrelated discussions, and search results often surface other workspace content to a guest who has 'access to one thing.' The inviter's mental model of 'I shared one ticket with this contractor' may not match what the guest can actually see.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
