      <Id>TH401</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Fabric Dataflow staged data and refresh history may persist sensitive intermediate values outside the controls applied to the final destination</ShortTitle>
      <Category>I</Category>
      <Description>Dataflow Gen2 stages data in OneLake-backed enhanced compute storage during transformation and writes incremental and refresh history. Intermediate columns dropped before the final write may still exist in staging, and refresh history may quote sample row values in error messages. The downstream destination's column-level controls do not protect data that never reaches it.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Dataflow Gen2 stages data in OneLake-backed enhanced compute storage during transformation and writes incremental and refresh history. Intermediate columns dropped before the final write may still exist in staging, and refresh history may quote sample row values in error messages. The downstream destination's column-level controls do not protect data that never reaches it.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
