      <Id>TH393</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Apache Airflow Web UI roles may grant DAG-trigger or connection-edit privileges that bypass code-review on automation</ShortTitle>
      <Category>E</Category>
      <Description>The Airflow web UI exposes role-based actions including triggering DAG runs with arbitrary configuration JSON, editing Connection and Variable values, and clearing/marking task instances. Users with broad UI roles (Op, Admin) can invoke production automation with crafted payloads, change credentials live, or rewrite task state, without going through the code-review path that governs DAG files.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value xsi:nil="true" />
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatDescription</Name>
          <Label>Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>The Airflow web UI exposes role-based actions including triggering DAG runs with arbitrary configuration JSON, editing Connection and Variable values, and clearing/marking task instances. Users with broad UI roles (Op, Admin) can invoke production automation with crafted payloads, change credentials live, or rewrite task state, without going through the code-review path that governs DAG files.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Priority</Name>
          <Label>Severity</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>High</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Priority</Description>
          <Id>22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>PossibleMitigations</Name>
          <Label>Possible Mitigation(s)</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Restrict UI roles using Airflow's RBAC: separate DAG authors, operators, and admins. Disable trigger-with-config for production DAGs that should run only on schedule. Scope Connection and Variable edit rights to a small named set. Audit UI actions and feed them to the same review surface that watches code changes.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>List of possbile mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>PossibleMitigations</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>SDLPhase</Name>
          <Label>SDL Phase</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Design</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>The Security Development Lifecycle Phase to be implemented.</Description>
          <Id>SDLPhase</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Documentation</Name>
          <Label>Documentation</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>https://airflow.apache.org/docs/apache-airflow/stable/security/access-control.html</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Link to documentation</Description>
          <Id>Documentation</Id>
          <AttributeType>0</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>Steps</Name>
          <Label>Steps</Label>
          <HideFromUI>false</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Enumerate UI roles assigned to each user. Confirm operators cannot edit production Connections or trigger sensitive DAGs with arbitrary config.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Description>Perscriptive guidance on how to implement mitigations.</Description>
          <Id>Steps</Id>
          <AttributeType>2</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
